---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Container from "@components/ui/Container.astro";
import Badge from "@components/ui/Badge.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "@components/seo/Breadcrumb.astro";

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: "Privacy Policy", url: "/privacy" }];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Quick JPG Converter"
  description="Quick JPG Converter privacy policy. Learn how we handle your data — or rather, how we don't. Your images never leave your browser."
  canonical="https://quickjpgconverter.com/privacy"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <section class="section">
    <Container variant="narrow">
      <Breadcrumb items={breadcrumbs} />

      <div class="mt-8">
        <Badge class="mb-4">Legal</Badge>
      </div>

      <article class="prose mt-6">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p><em>Last updated: June 9, 2026</em></p>

        <p>
          Quick JPG Converter ("we", "our", "us") is committed to protecting your
          privacy. This privacy policy explains how we handle data when you use our
          website and tools at <a href="https://quickjpgconverter.com">quickjpgconverter.com</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          By using our website, you agree to the practices described in this policy.
          If you do not agree, please discontinue use of our services.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3>1.1 Image Data</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>We do not collect, store, or transmit your images.</strong> All
          image processing happens entirely within your web browser using the Canvas
          API and client-side JavaScript. Your files never leave your device and are
          never uploaded to our servers or any third-party service.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you close the page or refresh, all image data is permanently erased
          from memory. We have no ability to access, recover, or view your images.
        </p>

        <h3>1.2 Automatically Collected Information</h3>
        <p>
          Like most websites, we automatically collect certain non-personal
          information when you visit our site. This may include:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser type and version</li>
          <li>Operating system</li>
          <li>Device type (desktop, tablet, mobile)</li>
          <li>Referring URL</li>
          <li>Pages visited and time spent on each page</li>
          <li>General geographic region (country/city level only)</li>
          <li>Date and time of visit</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This information is aggregated and anonymized. It cannot be used to
          identify individual users.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>

        <h3>2.1 Essential Cookies</h3>
        <p>
          We use only essential cookies required for the website to function
          properly. These include:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Theme preference</strong> — stores your dark/light mode choice in localStorage</li>
          <li><strong>Session cookies</strong> — required for basic site functionality</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2.2 Advertising Cookies</h3>
        <p>
          Our advertising partners (such as Google AdSense) may use cookies to
          serve relevant advertisements. These cookies are set by third-party ad
          networks and are subject to their respective privacy policies. You can
          manage your ad personalization preferences through your
          <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ad Settings</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>2.3 Analytics Cookies</h3>
        <p>
          We may use privacy-respecting analytics tools to understand how our
          website is used. These tools collect aggregated data such as page views,
          session duration, and general traffic patterns. No personally identifiable
          information is collected through analytics.
        </p>

        <h3>2.4 Managing Cookies</h3>
        <p>
          You can control and delete cookies through your browser settings. Please
          note that disabling essential cookies may affect the functionality of our
          website. To learn more about cookies, visit
          <a href="https://www.allaboutcookies.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">allaboutcookies.org</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
        <p>
          We use the automatically collected information for the following purposes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>To operate and maintain our website</li>
          <li>To analyze usage patterns and improve our tools</li>
          <li>To detect and prevent technical issues or abuse</li>
          <li>To serve relevant advertisements (see Section 5)</li>
          <li>To comply with legal obligations</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Data Sharing and Third Parties</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell, trade, or rent your personal information to third
          parties. We may share aggregated, non-identifiable data in the following
          limited circumstances:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Advertising partners</strong> — ad networks may collect data per their own privacy policies</li>
          <li><strong>Legal compliance</strong> — if required by law, court order, or governmental request</li>
          <li><strong>Business transfers</strong> — in the event of a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Since image processing happens entirely client-side, no image data is ever
          transmitted to any third party.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Google AdSense and Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          We use Google AdSense to display advertisements on our website. Google
          AdSense uses cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to our
          website and other websites on the internet.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve
          ads based on your visit to our site and/or other sites on the internet.
          You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting
          <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Third-party ad networks may also use technologies such as web beacons
          (pixels) to collect information about your visits to our site and other
          sites. This information is used to provide targeted advertisements.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Your Rights Under GDPR (EU Users)</h2>
        <p>
          If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA), the United
          Kingdom, or Switzerland, you have the following rights under data
          protection law:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Right to access</strong> — request a copy of the data we hold about you</li>
          <li><strong>Right to rectification</strong> — request correction of inaccurate data</li>
          <li><strong>Right to erasure</strong> — request deletion of your data</li>
          <li><strong>Right to restrict processing</strong> — request limitation of data processing</li>
          <li><strong>Right to data portability</strong> — receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format</li>
          <li><strong>Right to object</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Since we collect virtually no personal data, most of these rights are
          largely moot. However, if you wish to exercise any of these rights,
          contact us at
          <a href="https://mail.google.com/mail/?view=cm&fs=1&to=supportquickjpgconverter@gmail.com">supportquickjpgconverter@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your Rights Under CCPA (California Users)</h2>
        <p>
          If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act
          (CCPA) grants you the following rights:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Right to know</strong> — what personal information we collect and how it is used</li>
          <li><strong>Right to delete</strong> — request deletion of personal information</li>
          <li><strong>Right to opt out</strong> — opt out of the sale of personal information</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal information. To exercise your rights under the
          CCPA, contact us at
          <a href="https://mail.google.com/mail/?view=cm&fs=1&to=supportquickjpgconverter@gmail.com">supportquickjpgconverter@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Our website is not directed at children under the age of 13 (or 16 in the
          EEA). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If
          you believe a child has provided us with personal information, please
          contact us immediately so we can delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          We implement reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards
          to protect the information we collect. However, no method of transmission
          over the Internet or electronic storage is 100% secure. We cannot
          guarantee absolute security.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since all image processing happens client-side, your images are never at
          risk of being intercepted during transmission to our servers — because
          they are never transmitted in the first place.
        </p>

        <h2>10. International Data Transfers</h2>
        <p>
          Our servers are located in the United States. If you access our website
          from outside the US, your information may be transferred to and processed
          in the US. By using our website, you consent to such transfers.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Changes will be
          posted on this page with an updated revision date. We encourage you to
          review this policy periodically. Your continued use of our website after
          changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this privacy policy or our data practices,
          please contact us at:
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Email:</strong>
          <a href="https://mail.google.com/mail/?view=cm&fs=1&to=supportquickjpgconverter@gmail.com">supportquickjpgconverter@gmail.com</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          You may also visit our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> for additional
          contact options.
        </p>
      </article>
    </Container>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
